\[Charts\] Allow showing a visual indicator of data update, such as flash effect

**Context**

* Users want to indicate when the chart data has been updated.  
* Users want to indicate which data has been updated.  
  * Similar to [https://www.ag-grid.com/react-data-grid/change-cell-renderers/](https://www.ag-grid.com/react-data-grid/change-cell-renderers/)  
* Animation does help but this adds extra level of visual differentiation.  
* Other transitions can already be done by using chart update methods \- [https://plnkr.co/edit/RLeWLrV55qs9a2TX?open=main.js](https://plnkr.co/edit/RLeWLrV55qs9a2TX?open=main.js)

**Desired**

* When data is added/updated there is the option to flash it.  
  * Entire chart flashes.  
    * Over everything? Behind everything?  
  * The updated datapoint flashes / pulses.  
    * Series Specific  
  * The axis band is flashed  
    * cartesian charts only.  
    * band-scale axes only.  
* Options  
  * `flashOnUpdate:{}`  
    * `enabled: bool`  
    * `item: 'chart' | 'datum' | 'category'`  
    * `color: css string`  
    * `opacity: ratio`  
    * `flashDuration: ms`  
    * `fadeDuration: ms`

 

